quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  2,77,Do they not know that Allah is aware of whatever they conceal and whatever they reveal?
  2,78,There are some illiterate men among them (the Jews) who know nothing of the Book except lies and vague fancies. They rely only on assumption and speculation.
  2,79,"So, woe to those who write down the scripture with their hands and then claim, ‘This is from God,’ so they may sell it for a paltry gain. Woe to them for what their hands have written! Woe to them for what they have earned."
  2,80,"They say: ‘The Fire will never touch us except for a few days.’ Say: ‘Have you received a promise from Allah? If so, Allah will never break His promise. Or do you assert about Allah what you have no means to know?’"
  2,81,"Truly, whoever commits misdeeds and is surrounded by his evil, it is they who shall be the inmates of the Hellfire. They shall abide in it forever."
  2,82,"And those who believe and perform righteous deeds, it is they who shall be the residents of Paradise. They shall abide in it forever."
  2,83,"(Remember) when We took a pledge from the Children of Israel: ‘Worship none but Allah and behave excellently with (your) parents and near kinsfolk, and the orphans and the poor. Speak good words to all people. Establish prayer and pay the alms-due.’ Then all except a few of you turned away (from the pledge), and you are but averse (to the truth)."
